# Skill router

If several skills could apply, **choose one** (do not half-run two). Prefer the
more specific / safer gate.

| Signal in the message | Prefer | Not |
|----------------------|--------|-----|
| Unknown bug / flaky / wrong data / “broke” | `/fix` | `/make` |
| Clear new capability / “add X” with known shape | `/make` | `/fix` |
| UI demo / HTML clone / multi-todo screen build | `/plan` | `/feature`, `/fix` |
| Product feature + review-before-ship / migrations in slices | `/feature` | `/plan` (unless user wants `.plan.md` graph) |
| Want verdict only / pre-merge check | `/review` | `/make`, `/fix` |
| Commit / push / publish | `/ship` | implementing in same breath — finish work first |
| Remember / durable decision | `/note` | `/plan` for task graphs |
| Improve this pack’s skills | `/upgrades` | app `/make` |

**Same message combos**

- Code + “ก็ commit ด้วย” → finish `/make` or `/fix` first; then `/ship` (or ask to confirm ship).
- “Build UI and fix the bug” → if cause unclear, `/fix` first; else `/plan` with `/make`+`/fix` todos.
- Slash skill named explicitly → that skill wins over inference.
